/**
 * The degradation risk model (`docs/ML.md`). Runs once over the whole replay window and
 * persists one {@link RiskScore} per asset per day, so every API call is a cheap read.
 *
 * Method, per asset and day:
 * 1. Weather-normalized expected energy: degree-day regression (`a + b × CDD` for cooling,
 *    `a + b × HDD` for heating, both for air) fit on a trailing 60-day window ending 7 days
 *    before the scored day, so slow degradation never teaches the baseline that bad is normal.
 * 2. Per-signal z-score against the asset's own previous 30 days (floors: pressure 0.5 psi,
 *    flow 0.2%, ΔT 0.5 °F, vibration 0.1 mm/s, energy-pct 1.0), direction-adjusted so
 *    positive = bad, negatives clipped to 0, 3-day rolling mean.
 * 3. Weighted sum (pressure .25, flow .25, ΔT .15, vibration .15, energy .20, renormalized over
 *    non-null signals) × `(1 + age_years / 60)`, × 1.3 for heating when `tavg_f < 0`, × 1.2 for
 *    cooling when `tmax_f > 85`.
 * 4. Status per `docs/CONTRACT.md` §2 (`WATCH_THRESHOLD` 2.0, `PERSISTENCE_DAYS` 2, hysteresis,
 *    `FAILED` from {@link FailureEvent}s). A day with all signals missing carries the previous
 *    risk × 0.9 and never raises it.
 */
type RiskModel {
  /**
   * Score every asset for every day that has a {@link SensorReading}, replacing existing
   * {@link RiskScore} rows, at inspection `threshold` (default 3.0). Returns the number of rows written.
   */
  score_all: function(threshold: double): int py
}
